      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ARMOURY (7) made a winning start for Luke McCarthy last week, coming from a similar barrier and getting home by 1.3 metres at Penrith. That was her first outing for close to a year and just her second race start so she is open to improvement in both fitness and experience. Could go through her grades. BARRYS ROSE (6) is racing well, finishing runner-up in two of three starts here since a Tamworth win. Led from this barrier and went under narrowly here last time. Contender. SYLVIA KAY NZ (3) drew very wide at Menangle last start but had kicked off the campaign with back-to-back placings here so can bounce back aided by a good draw. LEAVE IT TO LUCY (10) may need some luck from the back row but she is racing well with a win and two placings from her last four attempts at Tamworth.",
